s":[],"digest":"bb755946ede029a7962710c09e8bbd0d91d65c1142481bce783d9c689894285b"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":20136,"output_tokens":1524,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"81f7b09a46252ddd2d4dda25b1929ae6e221e7e03f70434426c996c2b625cc55"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":54274,"output_tokens":1339,"requests":5}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"aa82303711e565570894949d0ec0c610c6be268232b8f545e99ca9289503f9a7"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":41710,"output_tokens":4550,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","verify command `ls` inspects output with `ls` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the default reply-reading protocol: read one newline-terminated line from proc.stdout per get-mark, strip it, and validate it as hex of the repo's object-id length.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.567,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"reads each 40-hex `get-mark` reply from `proc.stdout`\""],"finding":"The Approach says the fix 'reads each 40-hex get-mark reply from proc.stdout'. It does not say whether the reader consumes exactly 40 bytes or a full newline-terminated line. A fixed 40-byte read leaves the trailing newline in the stream, which corrupts the next reply. It also breaks on SHA-256 repositories, where the reply is 64 hex characters.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa34555ef78f6b09a","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach","norm_id":"n39bcac09775c8105","priority":0.033,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The executor implements read(40), and the leftover '\\n' shifts every later mark.","A repository uses objectformat=sha256, so the 64-hex reply is truncated."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Approach, replace '40-hex' with: 'read one line per get-mark reply via proc.stdout.readline(), strip the trailing newline, and validate it is a hex object id (40 or 64 chars) before use.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that an empty, short or non-hex get-mark reply from proc.stdout raises the existing stream-failure error, including fast-import's stderr, rather than being returned as a mark.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.917,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"reads each 40-hex `get-mark` reply from `proc.stdout`\"","test_stream_failure_raises_and_leaves_the_branch_unchanged is listed among the tests that must pass, but no new error contract for the stdout reader is stated."],"finding":"The plan does not say how the stdout reader behaves when fast-import exits or fails before replying. Reading proc.stdout then returns an empty or short result rather than an error. The plan does not require that this raise a stream failure; without that, an empty or partial mark could be used silently.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe7f474a748b9ba72","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Testing","norm_id":"n0eff6d5e7ee99abf","priority":0.033,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["fast-import rejects a malformed commit and exits, so the next get-mark readline() returns b''.","The empty value is passed on as a commit SHA."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to Approach: 'If the reply line is empty (EOF) or not a valid hex object id, raise the session's stream error with the process return code and stderr; test_stream_failure_raises_and_leaves_the_branch_unchanged continues to cover this.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the stdout reply reader tolerant of line endings (read one line, strip whitespace, check for 40 hex chars), and either dispatch sweep (windows) on the change before merge or say explicitly that AC3 is the first real Windows check.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"reads each 40-hex `get-mark` reply from `proc.stdout`\". Partially-verified: the git docs say replies go to stdout, but nothing was observed on Windows.","reclaim_collapse_stream.py:139-143: `while not buf.endswith(b\"\\n\"): chunk = os.read(self._marks, 41 - len(buf))`. This assumes exactly 41 bytes, LF-terminated.",".github/workflows/test.yml:262: sweep-windows runs only `if: github.event_name == 'schedule' || github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'`, so the change gets no Windows run before merge.","Testing section: the regression test wraps Popen to raise when pass_fds is non-empty. That proves pass_fds is gone, not that the stdout replies parse correctly on Windows."],"finding":"The plan's claim that fast-import's stdout behaves the same on Windows is never tested against real Git for Windows before merge, and the new stdout reader is not made robust to a CR byte before the LF in a reply. The regression test only fakes CPython's pass_fds assertion on the host platform, and the sweep (windows) job runs only on schedule or workflow_dispatch. So the first real Windows check of reading 40-hex replies from stdout is AC3, after merge. If the plan keeps the current byte-count reader (`os.read(..., 41 - len(buf))`, looping until the buffer ends with LF) and points it at proc.stdout, any CR before the LF in a reply would trigger a zero-length read and a false 'closed before returning a mark' error. That would only show up after the merge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f324ecad4be0ec5e8","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope: src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse_stream.py `_read_sha`; AC3","norm_id":"n8cdcfca3da995f00","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If Git for Windows writes a CR before the LF in a reply on stdout, the fixed byte-count read fails on Windows only, and AC3 then fails after the change has merged.","The Gerrit Verified +1 run passes on Linux or macOS, so nothing shows the problem until the scheduled or dispatched Windows sweep runs."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In `_read_sha`, read one line with `self._proc.stdout.readline()`. Treat an empty result as EOF and raise the existing 'closed before returning a mark' error. Otherwise strip it and check it is 40 hex characters. Replace `os.close(self._marks)` in close() and abort() with closing `self._proc.stdout`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_un